#Prior to all analysis, samples needed to be demultiplexed using guppy 
```{bash}
DATADIR=/Users/smagl/Desktop/ZoeAlbert/data_all
```
Putting this in a loop that will:
1. Make an output folder for the demux data.
2. Call on the individual outer barcode to demux.
3. Put that data into the output folder was just made.
```{bash}
for bc in {4..8};do # For the three outer barcodes used
~/ont-guppy-cpu/bin/guppy_barcoder \
-i ${DATADIR}/barcode0${bc}/ \
-s ${DATADIR}/demux_0${bc} \
--fastq_out --enable_trim_barcodes \
--config configuration_dual.cfg;done
```
